  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigation and adaptation through conservation and sustainable livelihoods in Indonesia&apos;s peat and mangrove ecosystems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peatland and mangrove ecosystems (PMEs) provide ecosystem services to communities in Indonesia in the form of coastal and flood protection, water quality and food security. The project supported the large-scale conservation and effective management of PMEs in West Papua and North Sumatra to increase the resilience of highly vulnerable communities and their biodiversity to the consequences of climate change. It relied on sustainable economic solutions such as crab fisheries, non-timber forest products and the agricultural utilisation of wet raised bogs and fens, which at the same time contribute to the development of alternative livelihoods. By avoiding the deforestation of 20000 hectares of mangroves and 60000 hectares of peat forests within the project duration, the project helped to save around 30 million tonnes of CO2eq. In total, around 10,000 people in the project areas benefit from the development of new sources of income through the sustainable utilisation of the PME.</narrative>
  </description>
